# Luau 0.742 (built from .data/projects/luau, CMake Release), Intel Xeon 2.1 GHz, 4 cores, 2026-10-15
# best of 7 per line; three process runs per mode
# an earlier version found the atom window by a linear scan back from the ring head: 2084.5 ns interpreted, 649.2 ns native (one run); replaced by the binary search below
## run 1 interpreted -O2
baseline: loop + slot lookup                                  25.7 ns/op  (sink 0)
cadence write (u16 ms, u16 key)                               91.9 ns/op  (sink 0)
aim write, code given (u16 ms, u16 key, 2 x u16)             132.3 ns/op  (sink 0)
aim write, direction -> yaw/pitch u16 (atan2, asin)          228.1 ns/op  (sink 0)
atom trigger (5 fields as f64, time, key, def)               162.9 ns/op  (sink 0)
atom complete (binary search + two-part copy, ~45 entries)   476.5 ns/op  (sink 0)
atom window entries copied (mean): 46
batch hand-off (16 atoms: exact buffer + frozen table)       702.9 ns/op  (sink 0)
memory per player: cadence ring 256 B per definition; aim ring 512 B; pending 448 B (8 slots); one atom 417 B (45 entries)
